<p>Use the following procedure to have the first sheet printed on a different 
 type of paper (for example, paper from a different paper tray) from the 
 other pages.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you use, this function may not be available.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Cover/Slip/Designate</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Front Cover</span> 
 check box, and then select the paper tray loaded with paper for the cover 
 sheet in the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span> 
 list, select the <a class="help-popup-link" data-help-popup="true" href="~/Topics/PCL_CS/IDH_CFRONT">print mode</a> 
 to use when printing the cover sheet.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Cover sheet 
 not printed on is not included in the print count.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to 
 use in the <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray</span> dialog 
 box when using bypass tray paper as the front cover sheet. </p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
